{
    "background_story": "Malaysia, a sleek and mysterious gymnorhina, or Australian magpie, lived in the sun-kissed outback. Her striking black and white plumage made her a standout among her peers. With a keen eye for shiny objects, Malaysia had a habit of collecting trinkets and treasures she found on her daily foraging expeditions. Her nest, a marvel of twigs and sparkles, was the envy of the other birds. But Malaysia's true claim to fame was her intelligence and problem-solving prowess. She had been observed using tools to extract food from hard-to-reach places, and even outsmarting predators with her cunning. As the seasons passed, Malaysia's legend grew, and she became a revered figure in the avian community, known for her wit, adaptability, and striking beauty.",
